  "chain_ok": true,
  "message": "`npm test` now passes: lint, typecheck, and all 256 tests exit 0.\n\nThere was one real failure, and the fix is a one-line correction to the test data, not to the library:\n\n- **The failure:** `building rotation 0` expected 14 triangles, but earcut returned 13.\n- **Why 14 is wrong:** the `building` fixture is a single simple 15-vertex ring with no holes. I checked that it has no self-intersections, and earcut returns 13 triangles with zero deviation. A simple polygon with n vertices always triangulates into exactly n−2 triangles, so 14 cannot be correct.\n- **The change:** `test/expected.json` now has `\"building\": 13`.\n\nThe lint step also failed at first because dependencies weren't installed. I ran `npm ci` to fix that; it doesn't change any tracked files. The only tracked change is `test/expected.json`.",
